            GameRoomRules.translate("- Do not add to entry 68: 76."),
            GameRoomRules.translate("Three wind pungs (38) exclude the non-value wind pung point (73) only for those same pungs. Other independent pungs may still score.")),
          rule_section(:table_mcr_payments, GameRoomRules.translate("MCR \u2014 Scoring and payments"),
            GameRoomRules.translate("Every opponent pays a base 8 points. On a discard win the discarder additionally pays the hand value including flowers; on self-draw every opponent adds that value. Each flower and season adds 1 fan to payment, but not to the 8-fan qualifying minimum.")),
          rule_section(:table_mcr_match, GameRoomRules.translate("MCR \u2014 Hands and match length"),
            GameRoomRules.translate("The default match has four wind rounds and exactly sixteen hands, with balances starting at zero. East, South, West and North each last four hands. The dealer always changes after a hand, so a dealer win or a draw does not add an extra repeat."),
            GameRoomRules.translate("Seat wind changes with the dealer, while round wind changes only after the four dealer periods. This changes which wind pungs score. Seasons remain separate bonus tiles. After each hand inspect the result and score; everyone must confirm readiness before the next hand."),
            GameRoomRules.translate("A draw gives no hand points in MCR. After all sixteen hands the highest balance wins; equal highest balances tie. Winning many small hands and losing one very expensive hand can still leave you behind, so a hand win and a match win are different goals.")),
          rule_section(:table_mcr_variants, GameRoomRules.translate("MCR \u2014 Match length options"),
            GameRoomRules.translate("Choose match length in the game options before play. The following shorter settings change how many hands the match contains, not the rules for completing a winning hand."),
            GameRoomRules.translate("One hand ends after one win or wall draw. Four wind rounds means sixteen hands: four with round wind East, four South, four West, four North. Within each round every player deals once. The dealer always advances, even after winning or a draw, so these sixteen hands do not grow through dealer repeats.")),
